{"id":1797,"level":73,"name":"Майстерня зв’язок","group":"Форсовані ходи","format":27,"description":"<p>A piece that is pinned is vulnerable. It cannot or should not leave and is therefore a desirable attacking target. We have seen that attacking a pinned piece is a clever method of exploiting a pin.</p>  <p>We encounter another way to take advantage of a pinned piece in this lesson. Because a pinned piece cannot (absolute pinning; king is the rear piece of the pinned piece) or may move (relative pinning; behind the pinned piece a piece or field is attacked), it is also a worthless defender. When a pinned piece cannot perform its defensive tasks, we have a pin party!</p>  <p>Let's move quickly to the examples.</p>  <p><strong>What do you have to do?</strong><br />Win material by capturing a piece defended by a pinned piece.</p>","assignment":"","stickerID":69,"examples":[{"fen":"7k/2q3np/p2p4/P2P1b2/2p5/2Q5/1P4PP/5RK1 w - - 0 1","pgn":"{[%cal Gc3h8,Rg7f5] [#]} 1. Rxf5 $1 *","text":"<p>кінь «захищає» слона, але оскільки коню заборонено рухатися (інакше король буде під контролем), захист нічого не вартий! Білі можуть просто взяти слона за допомогою<strong> 1.Rxf5!</strong></p>","format":27},{"fen":"r1b2rnk/pp4pp/3p4/3P4/5pP1/2B1q3/PP4BP/R1Q2R1K w - - 0 1","pgn":"{[%evp 0,3,732,790,834,841]} 1. Qxe3 {[%cal Gf1f8,Rf4e3]} fxe3 2. Rxf8 *","text":"<div id='solution'> <p>Чорного ферзя захищає пішак на f4. Проте цей захист не є оптимальним. Після <strong>1.Qxe3 fxe3</strong> білі можуть взяти туру: <strong>2.Rxf8</strong>. пішак захисту на f4 був зв’язаний.</p> </div>","format":27}],"puzzles":[{"id":40903,"fen":"4r1k1/5pp1/1p3n1p/p1qp4/3N4/1Pr1PQP1/P4P1P/R4RK1 b - - 0 1","pgn":"{[%cal Gc3f3,Re3d4]} {Q=1} 1... Qxd4 ! 2. exd4 Rxf3 *","format":27,"texts":["Зв’язані пішаки погано захищаються."],"text":"","isMulti":0,"multiThemes":[]},{"id":74798,"fen":"r1b2rk1/ppq1ppbp/n5p1/8/8/2P1BQ2/PP2BPPP/RN3RK1 w - - 0 1","pgn":"{[%cal Gf3a8,Rb7a6] [#]} {Q=1} 1. Bxa6 ! bxa6 2. Qxa8 *","form